<title>USA: Oneida to book $2 mln-$3mln post-tax Q1 gain.</title>
<headline>Oneida to book $2 mln-$3mln post-tax Q1 gain.</headline>
<dateline>ONEIDA, N.Y. 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oneida Ltd said on Wednesday that International Wire Group Inc bought its Camden Wire subsidiary for $60 million.</p>
<p>The sale will result in an after-tax gain for Oneida of $2 million to $3 million. The company said the gain would be included in the earnings for the 1997 first quarter that ends April 26, 1997.</p>
<p>Under the terms, International Wire of St Louis, Mo., will make a cash payment to Oneida of $44.5 million and assume Oneida's guarantee on $15.5 million in Camden Wire debt.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
